.Dd October 15, 2026
.Dt FORTI 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm forti
.Nd FortiOS from the command line
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Ar global-options
.Ar command
.Op Ar arguments
.Nm
.Cm configure
.Op Fl -profile Ar name Fl -host Ar host Op Ar options
.Nm
.Cm doctor
.Op Fl -profile Ar name
.Nm
.Cm home
.Op Cm migrate
.Nm
.Cm cert
.Cm create | show | remove
.Op Fl -profile Ar name
.Nm
.Cm profile
.Cm set | rename | copy
.Ar arguments
.Nm
.Cm get
.Ar resource
.Op Ar key
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
reads and changes FortiGate configuration through the FortiOS REST API.
It works with
.Em profiles :
named connection settings for a device, kept in
.Pa config.json
together with a reference to the device's API key.
The key itself is kept in the secret store, an environment variable or a command's output, never in
the configuration file and never on the command line.
.Pp
Text output is meant for people; with
.Fl -json
every command prints a stable JSON envelope,
.Dl {\(dqok\(dq: true, \(dqdata\(dq: ..., \(dqmeta\(dq: {...}}
or
.Dl {\(dqok\(dq: false, \(dqerror\(dq: {\(dqcode\(dq: ..., \(dqmessage\(dq: ..., \(dqdetails\(dq: {...}}}
and the exit status follows the error code (see
.Sx EXIT STATUS ) .
.Sh GLOBAL OPTIONS
Global options may appear before or after the command.
.Bl -tag -width "-p, --profile name"
.It Fl p , Fl -profile Ar name
Use this profile.
The default is the default profile, or the only one.
.It Fl -vdom Ar name
VDOM for this request.
.It Fl -json
Print the JSON result envelope.
Also
.Ev FORTI_OUTPUT Ns =json .
.It Fl -no-color
No ANSI colors.
Colors are used only when the output is a terminal and
.Ev NO_COLOR
is unset.
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Help for
.Nm
or for a command.
.It Fl -version
Print the version and the FortiOS version the models were generated from.
.El
.Sh COMMANDS
.Ss Setup
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm configure
Create or update a profile.
Without options it prompts on the terminal; the API key is typed with echo disabled.
The prompts also offer a client certificate: reuse one of forti's certificates, or make one and print
the FortiOS commands that make the FortiGate require it, before the connection check.
With options it runs without prompts:
.Bl -tag -width "--api-key-command cmd"
.It Fl -profile Ar name
Profile name (letters, digits,
.Ql -
and
.Ql _ ) .
Required with other options.
.It Fl -host Ar host
Host name or address, without scheme or port.
.It Fl -port Ar n
Admin HTTPS port (default 443).
.It Fl -vdom Ar name
Default VDOM for the profile.
.It Fl -ca-bundle Ar path
PEM CA bundle that verifies the device certificate.
.It Fl -resolve-ip Ar ip
Connect to this address while verifying the certificate for
.Ar host .
.It Fl -cert Ar name
One of forti's client certificates
.Pq Cm cert list ,
with its password.
.It Fl -client-cert Ar path
A PKCS#12 client certificate of your own.
.It Fl -api-key-stdin
Read the API key from standard input and keep it in the secret store.
.It Fl -api-key-env Ar var
Read the key from the environment variable
.Ar var
on every use; only the name is saved.
.It Fl -api-key-command Ar cmd
Run
.Ar cmd
(split like a shell, executed without one) and use the first line of its output.
.It Fl -cert-password-stdin , Fl -cert-password-env Ar var , Fl -cert-password-command Ar cmd
The client certificate's password, from the same kinds of source.
.It Fl -cert-password-file Ar path
Or from a file that only the user can read (mode 0600, not a symbolic link).
forti's own certificates use such a file.
.It Fl -mode Ar mode
.Cm read-only
(default),
.Cm guarded
or
.Cm autonomous ;
see
.Sx OPERATING MODES .
.It Fl -default
Make this the default profile.
.It Fl -skip-check
Save without contacting the device.
.El
.Pp
Before saving,
.Cm configure
reads
.Pa monitor/system/status
from the device.
If the read fails nothing is saved.
An authentication failure is not retried, because FortiOS locks out an API user after repeated
failures.
.Pp
On an existing profile the prompts start from its current values, and Enter keeps each one.
With options, only the options given change, for example
.Ql forti configure --profile fw01 --port 8443 .
.It Cm profile Op Cm list
List profiles; the default is marked with
.Ql * .
.Cm devices
is a short form.
.It Cm profile show Op Ar name
Show a profile and where its key comes from (never the key).
.It Cm profile set Ar name Ar key Ns = Ns Ar value ...
Change settings without contacting the device.
Keys:
.Cm host , port , vdom , ca_bundle , client_cert , resolve_ip , connect_timeout_ms , timeout_ms ,
.Cm backup_before_critical
.Pq Cm true | false
and
.Cm mode .
An empty value restores the default.
Values are validated as
.Pa config.json
is.
A changed host or port re-binds the profile's stored secrets to the new address.
.It Cm profile rename Ar old Ar new
Rename a profile.
Its stored secrets (Keychain or file store),
.Pa <home>/certs/ Ns Ar old ,
paths that point into that directory, and the default follow.
Plans made before the rename name the old profile.
.It Cm profile copy Ar source Ar new
Create a profile with the source's settings.
The API key reference, the client certificate and its password are not copied; run
.Nm
.Cm configure Fl -profile Ar new
next.
.It Cm profile default Ar name
Make
.Ar name
the default profile.
.It Cm profile mode Oo Ar name Oc Ar mode
Set the operating mode.
.It Cm profile remove Ar name
Delete the profile and its stored secrets.
.It Cm home
Print the forti home and every location in it, and flag a pre-0.2 setup.
.It Cm home migrate
Move a pre-0.2 setup
.Pf ( Pa ~/.config/forti ,
.Pa ~/.local/state/forti ,
.Pa ~/.cache/forti ,
or the
.Ev XDG_*_HOME
equivalents) into the home: config.json, credentials/, the state and the cache.
Moves are renames, so modes are kept; config.json moves last.
It never overwrites a config.json already in the home, and running it again is harmless.
Keychain items need no change.
.It Cm cert create Oo Ar name Oc Oo Fl -profile Ar profile Oc Oo Fl -own-ca Oc Oo Fl -days Ar n Oc Oo Fl -force Oc Op Fl -keychain
Create a client certificate for FortiOS PKI authentication of the REST API user, named
.Ar name
(CN
.Li forti- Ns Ar name ) ,
in
.Pa <home>/certs/ Ns Ar name Ns / :
.Pa ca.crt ,
.Pa client.crt ,
.Pa client.p12
and
.Pa client.pass
(0600).
Certificates need no profile; several profiles may use one.
It is issued by the forti CA,
.Pa <home>/ca/
(made on first use; a FortiGate imports it once), or with
.Fl -own-ca
by a CA of its own
.Pq Pa ca/ca.key , No 0600 .
Without
.Ar name
it is named after the default profile, which then uses it
.Pq Li default No when there is no profile ;
.Fl -profile
names the profile that uses it.
A profile's password is read from
.Pa client.pass
(or, with
.Fl -keychain ,
kept in the secret store of
.Fl -profile ) .
The PKCS#12 uses PBE-SHA1-3DES with a SHA-1 MAC, which OpenSSL 3, LibreSSL and FortiOS all read.
It prints the paths, the command that reads the password (never the password), and the FortiOS
commands, with the CA certificate inline, to import the CA
.Pq Li config vpn certificate ca ,
create a PKI user and peer group
.Pq Li config user peer , config user peergrp
and require the certificate for the API user
.Pq Li set peer-auth enable , set peer-group .
.Fl -days
sets the validity (default 1095).
An existing certificate is replaced only with
.Fl -force ;
one from the forti CA then needs no change on the FortiGate.
Needs the
.Xr openssl 1
command.
.It Cm cert list
The forti CA and every certificate: issuer, expiry and the profiles using it.
.It Cm cert show Op Ar name
Subject, issuer, expiry, SHA-256 fingerprint and files of a certificate (default: the one the selected profile uses).
.It Cm cert use Ar name Op Fl -profile Ar profile
Make a profile (default: the default profile) use a certificate.
.It Cm cert remove Op Ar name
Delete a certificate and detach it from every profile that used it.
.It Cm doctor
Run ordered checks: the forti home (a pre-0.2 setup is a warning), configuration directory and file modes, profile, secret resolution, CA bundle
and client certificate files, connection (DNS, TCP, TLS), authentication, FortiOS version against
the SDK schema, operating mode (for autonomous profiles also the API account's privileges), and whether
.Nm forti-mcp
is on
.Ev PATH .
Each is reported as ok, warn, fail, skip or info.
Exits 0 when nothing failed, otherwise with the status of the first failure.
.El
.Ss Read
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm devices
List profiles.
.It Cm discover Op Ar search | resource
Search the resource catalog, or show a resource's attributes
.Pq Fl -kind , Fl -fields , Fl -live , Fl -start , Fl -count .
.It Cm get Ar resource Op Ar key
Read configuration or monitor data
.Pq Fl -filter , Fl -fields , Fl -start , Fl -count , Fl -param .
Device secrets are shown as
.Dq <redacted> ;
.Fl -reveal
shows them on a terminal, or with
.Fl -json .
.El
.Ss Changes
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm plan set | create | delete | action | Fl -file Ar file Op Fl -apply
Write a stored plan: read the device, validate, and record the diff and the exact request.
The device is not changed.
.Cm create
takes
.Ar attr Ns = Ns Ar value
pairs or
.Fl -object .
.Fl -apply
applies the plan in the same command, as the profile's mode allows.
.It Cm plan show | approve Op Ar id
Show a plan, or approve it (guarded mode; at a terminal
.Cm approve
then offers to apply it).
.It Cm plan list
Stored plans, newest first.
.It Cm apply Op Ar id
Execute a plan once.
In guarded mode, at a terminal, it shows the plan and asks for the approval.
.It Cm rollback Op Ar id
Apply the rollback plan of the last applied plan (or of
.Ar id ) .
.El
.Pp
A plan
.Ar id
may be shortened to a unique prefix of the id or of its last part, or be
.Cm latest .
At a terminal,
.Cm show ,
.Cm approve
and
.Cm apply
without an id take the newest plan waiting to be applied, and show it first.
Without a terminal a plan must be named.
.Ss Integrations
.Cm install
and
.Cm mcp
are described by
.Nm
.Ar command
.Fl -help .
.Sh OPERATING MODES
The FortiOS account's privileges are the primary authorization boundary.
A profile's mode is the operator's policy on top of it:
.Bl -tag -width autonomous
.It Cm read-only
Reads and plan previews only; every apply is refused.
The default.
.Nm
.Cm profile mode Ar name Cm guarded
allows changes.
.It Cm guarded
A change is applied only after a person approves the exact plan: at a terminal when
.Nm
.Cm apply
asks, or with
.Nm
.Cm plan approve Ar id .
.It Cm autonomous
Changes are applied without interactive approval.
The agent can do anything the API account may do.
Validation, drift checks, verification, audit records and rollback plans still apply.
Scope the account's admin profile and trusted hosts to what the agent should manage.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width FORTI_SECRET_STORE
.It Ev FORTI_HOME
The forti home (default
.Pa ~/.forti ;
an absolute path).
.It Ev FORTI_CONFIG_DIR
Configuration directory (default: the home).
.It Ev FORTI_STATE_DIR
Plans, approvals, backups and the audit log (default
.Pa <home>/state ) .
.It Ev FORTI_CACHE_DIR
Cache (default
.Pa <home>/cache ) .
.It Ev XDG_CONFIG_HOME , XDG_STATE_HOME , XDG_CACHE_HOME
Used only to find a pre-0.2 setup, which stays in use until
.Cm home migrate .
.It Ev FORTI_SECRET_STORE
.Cm file
or
.Cm keychain .
Default: the macOS Keychain on macOS, the file store elsewhere.
.It Ev FORTI_OUTPUT
.Cm json
prints the JSON envelope for every command.
.It Ev NO_COLOR
Disables colors.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa ~/.forti/
The forti home (mode 0700).
.It Pa ~/.forti/config.json
Profiles; mode 0600.
Contains no secrets.
.It Pa ~/.forti/credentials/
The file secret store: one 0600 file per secret.
.It Pa ~/.forti/state/
Plans, approvals, pre-change backups and
.Pa audit.jsonl .
.It Pa ~/.forti/certs/ Ns Ar name Ns /
Client certificates
.Pq Cm cert list .
.It Pa ~/.forti/ca/
The forti CA that issues them; its key never leaves the machine.
.It Pa ~/.config/forti/ , ~/.local/state/forti/
A pre-0.2 setup, used until
.Cm home migrate
moves it.
.It Login Keychain, service Dq forti
The macOS secret store, accounts
.Ar profile Ns /api-key
and
.Ar profile Ns /cert-password .
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width 3n -compact
.It 0
success
.It 1
internal error
.It 2
usage error
.It 3
configuration: missing or invalid profile, credentials or config file
.It 4
connection (DNS, connect, TLS, timeout) or authentication (HTTP 401/403)
.It 5
not found: unknown object or resource
.It 6
validation or other FortiOS error
.It 7
refused: read-only mode, missing approval, or stale plan
.It 8
partial failure or unknown outcome of a change
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Configure a device, check it, and read its firewall policy:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
forti configure
forti doctor
forti get firewall/policy --fields policyid,name,action,status
.Ed
.Pp
Use a client certificate as well as the API key:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
forti cert create --profile fw01      # or answer y in forti configure
forti cert use fw01 --profile fw02    # a second FortiGate, same certificate
.Ed
.Pp
A second device with the same settings:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
forti profile copy fw01 fw02
forti profile set fw02 host=fw02.example.net
forti configure --profile fw02
.Ed
.Pp
Configure from a password manager without prompts:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
op read op://ops/fw01/api-key | forti configure --profile fw01 \e
    --host fw01.example.net --ca-bundle ~/fw01-ca.pem --api-key-stdin
.Ed
.Sh SECURITY
TLS certificate verification is always on; no option disables it.
Use
.Fl -ca-bundle
for self-signed or private-CA devices, and
.Fl -resolve-ip
to connect to an address while verifying the certificate's name.
Secrets are never accepted as arguments and never printed.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr forti-mcp 1
.Pp
.Lk https://github.com/valkyrianlabs/forti-cli
